1:diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
5:@@ -1,163 +1,194 @@
82:+The macOS-only `mtu-matrix` subcommand runs a bounded, loopback-only physical
83:+baseline across MTU 1500/4096/8500, IPv4/IPv6/dual stack, and nominal,
84:+constrained-buffer, receiver-stall, and mixed bidirectional traffic. Its
85:+configuration requires a task-scoped output below `.temp/` (or `/tmp`) and
86:+limits each row to 64...2048 packets:
88:+```bash
89:+swift run ReluxTunnelHarness mtu-matrix --configuration .temp/TASK-ID/matrix-config.json
90:+```
92:+At the 64-packet floor, each half of a dual-stack receiver-stall row uses the
93:+same measured 4096-byte fault-injection ceiling as constrained-buffer traffic;
94:+larger receiver-stall samples request 32768 bytes. This keeps the lower bound a
95:+real bounded queue-pressure run instead of depending on whether 32 packets fit
96:+in the larger queue.
98:+Output containment is bound during configuration parsing by traversing from a
99:+filesystem-root descriptor with `O_DIRECTORY | O_NOFOLLOW`, retaining every
100:+directory descriptor through the atomic temporary-file write, and rejecting a
101:+later path traversal whose device/inode chain no longer matches. This covers
102:+root symlinks, output-parent replacement, and swaps of ancestors above `.temp`.
104:+The report records attempted/sent/received packets, sender refusals and receive
105:+queue drops separately, bytes, `logicalBatchGroups` derived as ceil(sent/32),
106:+p50/p95 latency, packet and byte rates, CPU, requested/effective buffers,
107:+syscall counts, maximum successful datagram, fragmentation observation, and
108:+production-owned descriptor recovery. Swift-task lifecycle is explicitly
109:+unavailable because the synchronous runner owns no tasks; process threads are
110:+not used as a proxy. The command never configures a VPN, route, DNS, interface,
111:+or NetworkExtension.
